Kodi 22 has no "hidden" setting type, so the three settings declared with it
are never created:

  error <CSettingGroup>: unknown setting type "hidden" of "launchscript_conf"
  error <CSettingGroup>: unable to create new setting "launchscript_conf"

launchscript_conf is how Luna remembers which launch script to run, so
ConfigHelper reads back an empty string, launchscripts_path stays None, and
picking a game does nothing at all - the app list appears, the selection is
accepted, and no stream ever starts. It also re-asks which launch script to
use on every entry, because the answer can never be stored.

A string setting marked not visible is the supported way to keep a value out
of the settings UI.
---
diff --git a/resources/settings.xml b/resources/settings.xml
--- a/resources/settings.xml
+++ b/resources/settings.xml
@@ -242,14 +242,23 @@
                         <close>true</close>
                     </control>
                 </setting>
-                <setting id="addon_version" type="hidden" help="">
+                <setting id="addon_version" type="string" help="">
                     <level>0</level>
+                    <visible>false</visible>
+                    <default></default>
+                    <control type="edit" format="string"/>
                 </setting>
-                <setting id="last_run" type="hidden" label="30045" help="">
+                <setting id="last_run" type="string" label="30045" help="">
                     <level>0</level>
+                    <visible>false</visible>
+                    <default></default>
+                    <control type="edit" format="string"/>
                 </setting>
-                <setting id="launchscript_conf" type="hidden" label="30045" help="">
+                <setting id="launchscript_conf" type="string" label="30045" help="">
                     <level>0</level>
+                    <visible>false</visible>
+                    <default></default>
+                    <control type="edit" format="string"/>
                 </setting>
             </group>
         </category>
